# Original four-family prospective analysis

`metrics.py` implements fixed-cohort arithmetic for the original 32 primary and
28 one-factor trajectories. `numerical_contract_v1.json` preserves its estimands
and accounting rules before model outcomes. This is analysis preparation, not
an executed repository study or qualified live-receipt adapter.

`qualification-v1` passes 44 checks, including 20 malformed-export rejections.
All input outcomes, receipts, durations and calls in these controls are explicitly
synthetic. They are never paper repair observations. The retained source archive
and fixture permit exact reproduction without calling any model or grader.

The engine counts six required event outcomes per trajectory and separately
meters horizon0 setup/prime. Initial repair, eventual repair, final repair and
complete operational success are distinct. Every required obligation must match
its frozen inventory. Unknown independent plan coverage cannot pass, and an
unreached stale/recovery boundary cannot pass vacuously. A later successful repair
does not rewrite the initial failure. Zero-success ratios remain undefined.

Provider totals are authoritative. Input/output/reasoning/cache fields are not
summed to synthesize totals. Unknown possible dispatch/usage remains unknown;
known subtotals do not replace it. Exact repeated receipt aliases are counted
once, while orphan costs, duplicate authoritative records and cross-event
misattribution reject. Unique enclosing invocation intervals include interrupted
and resumed work; nested stage clocks are separate breakdowns. Host and container
CPU remain separate, and absent measurements are not zeroed.

Every primary B/C/D profile compares to A at the same cache setting. Each warm
one-factor control compares to its corresponding full B/D profile. The reported
fraction is `1 - treatment_tokens / baseline_tokens`; for component controls the
treatment is the disabled/additive/template variant, so positive does not mean
that the removed component helped. Unconditional spending differences remain
visible even if quality fails. Conditional descriptive reduction requires every
pair to complete the trajectory with an independently valid initial repair.
No population noninferiority follows from that observed gate.

The exact family bootstrap uses 256 four-family resamples (four two-family draws
for the first tranche), preserving all dependent event/cache observations in a
family. It is descriptive development uncertainty, not a power calculation or
360 independent tasks. Observed cumulative break-even includes prime costs and
requires non-higher token expenditure at every remaining measured horizon under
the complete-quality gate; no future horizon is extrapolated.

Before live use, an independently qualified file adapter must bind this engine
to the actual caller profile and original receipts. The current prospective
caller interface is `original_caller_output_contract_v2.json`. `make_schedule`
constructs identities/horizons from corpus v3, but actual required obligation IDs
must come from the frozen caller. The fixture's synthetic obligation must never
be used as that inventory. No model dispatch is enabled by this preparation.
